+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-11  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 10-15
+
+---
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+  |
+  v
+E001 Transcript Review ──> E002 Confirmed Reminders
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### Pilot MVP Epics
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure — makes the small pilot build testable and repeatable.
+- E001: Transcript Review — owns the product's primary controlled review path and workspace isolation.
+- E002: Confirmed Reminders — completes the promised one-reminder delivery path and delivery status.
+
+No enhancement or future epic is planned. The four-week pilot is deliberately limited to the two product slices above.
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: Gives the two-engineer pilot a repeatable way to check, configure, and deliver the Python API and browser UI before product work depends on them.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Establish local test and build commands, CI checks, linting/formatting, environment and secret-handling conventions, and a minimal deployment/error-observation path appropriate to the pilot. It does not add product behavior or claim a production deployment exists.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A contributor can run the relevant API/UI checks locally with documented commands.
+- [ ] CI runs lint, tests, and build checks for planned product changes.
+- [ ] Environment configuration keeps provider credentials out of source control and supports a configurable provider later.
+- [ ] Failures in the pilot path have an observable development or runtime signal.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Repository, test, lint, and build baseline.
+- CI workflow and failure reporting.
+- Environment configuration and secrets conventions.
+- Pilot deployment/observation baseline.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None.
+- **Enables**: E001 and E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: Test and configuration seams only; no product domain model.
+- Files/Components: Repository tooling, CI configuration, environment examples, API/UI test configuration.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3-4  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+### E001: Transcript Review
+
+**Value Statement**: Enables facilitators to turn an uploaded workspace transcript into reviewed actions, so no action is scheduled before its text, owner, and due date are explicitly confirmed.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Deliver workspace-scoped transcript upload, proposed-action extraction, review, correction, and the confirmation gate. This epic owns the cross-workspace access boundary for transcripts and actions as well as PRM-001, PRM-002, and PRM-004.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and see proposed action items for that workspace.
+- [ ] Scheduling cannot proceed until the facilitator explicitly confirms action text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] Corrections made during review become the confirmed action values.
+- [ ] A negative probe using the real request role cannot read another workspace's transcripts or actions.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace-scoped transcript intake and storage.
+- Proposal extraction and review presentation.
+- Explicit field-by-field confirmation and incomplete-state handling.
+- Workspace authorization and real-role isolation test.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000.
+- **Enables**: E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: Workspace-scoped transcript, proposal, and confirmed-action persistence as chosen during epic planning.
+- Models/Services: Transcript intake, action-proposal extraction, confirmation, workspace authorization.
+- Files/Components: Browser transcript upload and facilitator review/confirmation surfaces; Python API endpoints and tests.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 5-7  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot MVP  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+### E002: Confirmed Reminders
+
+**Value Statement**: Enables facilitators to close the loop on a confirmed action with one configured-provider reminder and visible delivery status.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Build the configurable reminder-provider seam, send exactly one reminder for a confirmed action, and expose its delivery status in the facilitator experience. Provider choice is intentionally deferred; this epic must not expand into calendars, autonomous messaging, or reminder sequences.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A workspace can configure the provider used for the pilot reminder path.
+- [ ] A confirmed action can trigger exactly one reminder through that provider.
+- [ ] The facilitator can see the resulting delivery status.
+- [ ] Runtime evidence exercises upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery end to end.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Configurable provider contract and credentials wiring.
+- One-time send orchestration from a confirmed action.
+- Delivery-status capture and browser presentation.
+- End-to-end runtime evidence for the complete controlled path.
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001.
+- **Enables**: Pilot evaluation against delivery and review metrics.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: Reminder configuration and delivery-status persistence as chosen during epic planning.
+- Models/Services: Provider adapter, one-time reminder orchestration, delivery-status recording.
+- Files/Components: Provider configuration and delivery-status surfaces; Python API integration and end-to-end tests.
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3-4  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot MVP  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Foundation
+
+**Goal**: Make feature work repeatable and observable for the pilot.
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure.
+
+**Success Gate**: Local and CI checks can exercise the API/UI baseline, and configuration can safely accommodate the later provider integration.
+
+### Phase 1: Controlled Review Path
+
+**Goal**: Let facilitators review transcript-derived actions within a protected workspace boundary.
+
+- E001: Transcript Review, after E000.
+
+**Success Gate**: The explicit confirmation rule and cross-workspace negative probe both pass.
+
+### Phase 2: Reminder Closure
+
+**Goal**: Complete the promised path with one visible reminder attempt.
+
+- E002: Confirmed Reminders, after E001.
+
+**Success Gate**: Runtime evidence covers upload through delivery, and a facilitator can see delivery status.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Pilot work becomes hard to verify | Establish test, CI, configuration, and observation basics first |
+| E001 | Incorrect extraction or cross-workspace access erodes trust | Keep extraction reviewable, require explicit confirmation, and prove isolation with the real request role |
+| E002 | Unselected provider or scope creep delays the pilot | Use a configurable provider seam and restrict delivery to one reminder |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| E000 | Repeatable engineering checks | Relevant API/UI checks run locally and in CI | Command and CI evidence |
+| E001 | Proposal review rate and workspace isolation | >=80% review; no cross-workspace read | Pilot usage data; real-role negative probe |
+| E002 | Delivery-path completion | Every pilot attempt has visible status | Runtime end-to-end evidence and delivery records |
+
+## Planning Notes
+
+- This Build-level plan has two product epics, so the >=4-epic concurrency-wave and project-analysis gates do not apply.
+- Epics are sequential because E002 consumes the confirmed action owned by E001. Parallel execution is not planned.
+- Detailed specifications, technical approaches, provider selection, and validation artifacts are deferred to their canonical later phases.
